# Generated scan output and reports.
#
# SentinelAI writes its reports wherever --output points, which during
# development and demos is usually the repository root. None of it is source:
# every file matched here is reproducible by re-running the commands in
# sentinelai-manual-test/README.md, and the measurements derived from these
# artifacts are recorded in POLISH_REPORT.md rather than by committing the
# raw JSON.
#
# sentinelai-cli/.gitignore covers the same patterns for scans run from inside
# the package directory; this file covers scans run from the repository root.
scan-result*.json
sentinelai-cli-scan*.json
ai-latency-run*.json
sentinelai-report*.html
sentinelai-report*.md
*.sarif
report.json
report.md
report.html

# Docker run output. sentinelai-cli/README.md's documented container
# commands mount ./sentinelai-output as the writable /output target, so a
# normal `docker run` leaves this directory behind in whatever repository
# was scanned - including this one.
sentinelai-output/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store

# ── Research artifacts — local working files, never published ───────────
#
# Paper drafts, phase-by-phase editing reports, benchmark run outputs and
# the capstone report. These are research and editing artifacts produced
# while writing up the project; they are not part of the application and
# must not reach the remote.
#
# Deliberately NOT matched, and verified still tracked after these rules:
#   README.md, sentinelai-cli/README.md, sentinelai-manual-test/README.md,
#   sentinelai-cli/docs/CONTRACTS.md, sentinelai-cli/docs/prompts_appendix.md,
#   all source, tests, fixtures and scanner data files.
#
# Checked before adding: no .pdf/.docx/.doc/.tex/.png/.jpg/.svg is tracked
# on any local or remote branch, so the document and figure rules below
# cannot hide an existing or incoming project asset. core.ignorecase is
# true here, so every rule ends in an explicit extension - that is what
# keeps PHASE_*.md from reaching tests/test_phase5_e2e.py.

# Paper sources and exports, at any depth.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf
*.tex
*.bbl
*.aux
*.synctex.gz

# Research-paper directories. Root-anchored: a "papers" directory inside
# the application tree would be something else and stays tracked.
/research papers/
/research-papers/
/research_papers/

# Phase-by-phase editing and research-progress reports, at any depth.
PHASE_*.md
BENCHMARK_REPORT.md
FINAL_TECHNICAL_AUDIT.md
*_EDIT_PLAN.md
*_EDIT_REPORT.md
*_CHANGELIST.md
*_RECONSTRUCTION_REPORT.md
*_VISUAL_REPORT.md
*_LANGUAGE_REPORT.md

# The capstone report, in whichever format it is exported to.
SentinelAI_Capstone_Report.*

# Benchmark run outputs and generated paper figures. Root-anchored so a
# future benchmark fixture directory inside the package is unaffected.
/benchmarks/
/figures/

# Already tracked, so these two rules are INERT until the files are
# untracked with `git rm --cached`. Listed here so that protection takes
# effect the moment that happens - .gitignore alone cannot stop Git from
# publishing a file it is already tracking.
/PAPER_RESULTS.md
/POLISH_REPORT.md

# Local environment files at the repository root. sentinelai-cli/.gitignore
# already covers sentinelai-cli/.env; the root was not covered, so a .env left
# here was untracked but NOT ignored - one `git add -A` away from being
# published. Root-anchored so only these two paths are matched.
#
# /.env.* would also match the .env.example template, so it is negated back
# in: the template carries no values and must stay visible to Git even if it
# is ever removed from the index.
/.env
/.env.*
!/.env.example
